    <section class="block" id="summary">
      <div class="section-head"><span class="section-dot"></span><span class="section-label">Summary</span></div>
      <div class="callout">
<p><strong>Polymer scientist and R&D engineer</strong> with <span id="years"></span> years of experience developing materials that are difficult to formulate, difficult to process, and often considered impractical until they work.</p>
<script>document.getElementById('years').textContent=new Date().getFullYear()-2008;</script>
<p>My work has ranged from electrorheological suspensions, elastomers, silicone insulators, and wood–polymer composites to biodegradable food-contact packaging based on natural fillers. Regardless of the material system, the challenge has always been the same: understanding why a material behaves the way it does, finding practical solutions, and turning laboratory concepts into reliable manufacturing processes.</p>

<p>Over the years, I've built laboratories from the ground up, established and led multidisciplinary R&D teams, developed new formulations, commissioned production equipment, supported technology transfer, and worked closely with manufacturing, customers, and research partners. My background combines polymer physics, rheology, materials science, and industrial process development, allowing me to move comfortably between laboratory research and factory floors.</p>

<p>In recent years, my work has also included regulatory aspects of sustainable food-contact materials, including compliance with EU food-contact legislation, PPWR, and practical implementation of material qualification and documentation for industrial and customer validation.</p>

<p>This website is a collection of projects I've worked on, lessons learned along the way, and the people who made those projects possible.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
